#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:5
#: d49ab16f614d4f568392d4f6b04eb75c
msgid "ESC (Electronic Speed Controls)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:7
#: 80c53b753b204b859e581b214a41dc71
msgid "ESCs are available for either brushed (DC) or brushless (AC) motors. :ref:`Brushed motors<common-brushed-motors>` are most commonly used in toy-class planes, multicopters, rovers, boats, and balance bots. Most other larger vehicles use brushless speed controllers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:9
#: 80dab52e67e340e3a10c8413851ac825
msgid "ESCs are available in a confusing array of communication protocols, programming capability, telemetry, and multi unit configurations. Below is a guide to some of the terms and capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:12
#: 2160ee7d58ff4a8cabea26583254e220
msgid "Control Connection To Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:14
#: 0f612fbd34e142f3a47f5bee0161adc3
msgid "Single signaling wire to autopilot servo/motor output which can use pulse or digital communication protocols"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:15
#: b2842b9cdcab440c878b7fa46852a2b6
msgid ":ref:`DroneCAN <common-uavcan-escs>` or CAN, which provides a more robust connection with greater length limits at the expense of more wiring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:18
#: 321304937d184c1494b0c1c47a033976
msgid "Communication Protocols"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:20
#: 5263d5375da84afd8205c4b83670a91a
msgid "The ESC may be compatible with one or more of the following protocols:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:22
#: 985c90760e844ee5a7db6034c3255a32
msgid ":ref:`PWM, OneShot, OneShot125<common-brushless-escs>` are pulse based protocols. Almost all ESCs are compatible with PWM signaling. And this is the default configuration of ArduPilot firmware for servo/motor outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:23
#: 8c94093a1f424664852c631ef1e7505a
msgid ":ref:`DShot<common-dshot-escs>` is a digital protocol in which the speed is encoded as digital commands to the ESC. Speed of the signaling can be DShot150, DShot300, etc. depending on the ESC's capability. Other ESC commands for ESC led control, etc. can be sent to the ESC if it has the capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:24
#: e19dbb23055e49e5ab71cbfa375de759
msgid ":ref:`Bi-Directional DShot<bidir-dshot>` is a variation of Dshot that allows the ESC to return to the autopilot telemetry data. What type of data is ESC dependent. Sometimes referred to as BDShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:25
#: 485256e14f494a6a9ccd317662b9fca4
msgid ":ref:`FETtec OneWire<common-fettec-onewire>` ESC is another bi-directional protocol that sends speed commands and returns telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:28
#: f9f3cd23103b4a68a1c1aa031d9effa9
msgid "Telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:30
#: cfaa022f72e5434facb5252ee2cbabcf
msgid "As stated above some ESCs have the ability to return telemetry from the ESC. In addition to the Bi-Directional DShot and FETTec protocols, some DroneCAN/CAN ESCs have this capability. Some ESCs can provide motor RPM telemetry via an additional wire that is connected to the autopilot on one of its UART ports. See :ref:`common-esc-telemetry` for more info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:33
#: 151c9fbe20cf4001a07040f5fb087b38
msgid "ESC Programming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:35
#: e0b339889e7e47589f4bf8d48c0c9bfd
msgid "The ESC sometimes has parameters which can be programmed: timing, motor direction, battery cutoff, startup ramp, etc. Depending on the individual ESC, these can be programmed in different ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:37
#: b6d08a15d31a4abba37183d871ff1435
msgid "some via a sequence of throttle commands after entering a programming mode upon startup. These vary widely, ESC to ESC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:38
#: e181e64e510143198e6da4ba37b32743
msgid "some via an interface program like :ref:`BLHeli<common-blheli32-passthru>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:39
#: 083aa7041a754beea5714172afbbad0e
msgid "DroneCAN ESCs via DroneCAN parameters using the :ref:`DroneCAN GUI<common-uavcan-gui>` or Mission Planner's SETUP->Optional Hardware->DroneCAN/UAVCAN setup window to access the parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-guide.rst:40
#: 59cf1d0ea20c4a838cffd0dc207d384e
msgid "some use a supplied setup software program"
msgstr ""
